      "source": [
        "## How to prompt Omni\n",
        "\n",
        "Omni rewards a **modular** prompt, not a rigid template. Describe as many of these as matter,\n",
        "and the more detail you give, the more control you get:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Shot and motion**: framing and camera move (for example, \"locked-off wide\", \"slow push-in\").\n",
        "- **Style**: the look (cinematic, grounded, claymation, neon data-viz).\n",
        "- **Lighting**: source and quality (warm, crisp, ethereal).\n",
        "- **Location**: the setting.\n",
        "- **Action**: subjects, objects, and what they do.\n",
        "- **Audio**: ambience, sound effects, or dialogue, in plain language.\n",
        "\n",
        "Two principles that make Omni different from one-shot models:\n",
        "1. **Lean on its world knowledge.** You do not have to over-explain a concept or a physical\n",
        "   process; describe the intent and let it reason.\n",
        "2. **Edit by talking.** Generate once, then refine in conversation; it preserves what works\n",
        "   and changes only what you ask."
      ]
    },
